# fleetclient/manifest — the files a colleague's computer gets from the hub
# (claude-fleet#1470, #1486): `curl -fsSL <hub>/install | sh`.
#
# One repo-relative path per line, in install order; `#` starts a comment. Each
# is served at GET /install/<path> (its SHA-256 in X-Ccquota-Sha256) and lands
# at <install home>/<path> (~/.local/share/claude-fleet by default) — the repo's
# own bin/ + conf/ layout, so `$BIN/../conf/…` resolves there as in a checkout.
# The one line tagged `installer` is the template GET /install serves with the
# hub's URL filled in; it is never a download of its own.
#
# This list is read in three places and maintained here only:
#   · fleetclient/embed.go       the hub — what to serve, which file is the installer
#   · bin/fleet-client-mirror.sh the copy bin/ + conf/ → fleetclient/, and --check
#   · bin/fleet-install.sh       fetches it as GET /install/manifest and walks it
# and two tests hold the copies to the originals: TestFleetClientMatchesBin (Go)
# and bin/fleet-install-selftest.sh leg A (shell).
#
# What is on it: `fleet` and the two it dispatches to (#1470), plus the SHELL
# (#1484) — bin/fleet-shell.sh and everything it runs on the person's own
# computer, the set verified by running bin/fleet-shell-selftest.sh from a root
# holding only these files (101 checks). fleet-lib.sh ships whole: the row
# producer and the hub loop source it unconditionally, and a second lib for the
# shell would be a second code path in the render loop (EPIC #1479 「两套行生成
# 器漂移」). What a fleet NODE needs — spawning, reaping, the daemons, gh — stays
# out: the shell's rows are all remote, their actions all hub writes.
# bin/fleet-client-lib.sh rides along for the installer itself (#1629): its
# tmux step sources the lib's fc_tmux_ok / fc_pkg_install once downloaded.
# bin/fleet-node.sh + bin/fleet-node-join.sh are `fleet node join` (#1627): the
# one command that turns THIS computer into a node — a scan, then the join
# script's steps (which install the node's own tooling from git themselves).
